      "text": "To determine the value of \\( a \\) for which \\( g(a) = 0 \\) for the function \\( g(x) = 3x - 4 \\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Substitute \\( g(x) \\) into the equation \\( g(a) = 0 \\)**:\n   \\[\n   g(a) = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. **Write down the function definition \\( g(x) = 3x - 4 \\)**:\n   \\[\n   3a - 4 = 0\n   \\]\n\n3. **Solve for \\( a \\)** by isolating the variable \\( a \\):\n   \\[\n   3a - 4 = 0\n   \\]\n\n4. Add \\( 4 \\) to both sides of the equation:\n   \\[\n   3a = 4\n   \\]\n\n5. Divide both sides by \\( 3 \\):\n   \\[\n   a = \\frac{4}{3}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( a \\) for which \\( g(a) = 0 \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{4}{3}}\\).",
